{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld","id":1055157,"title":"An Exigent of Chaos/Wyld?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-26T03:23:01-08:00","id":1055157,"title":"An Exigent of Chaos/Wyld?","content":"So I've been ruminating a bit after reading some of Graceful Wicked Masques and wondered -- hey, the Fair Folk have charms. Can they make Exalted?<br /> <br /> Well no, duh, right? Then Ex3 comes in with the whole plotline of Exigence and black market exaltations and I wondered (once again) -- can the Fair Folk use Exigence to create Exalted of their own?<br /> <br /> From what I've read, there hasn't been anything explicit regarding whether Exigence can only be used by a God (unless there has been something explicit about that, then *sweat droopy*). If it is only usable by a God, would there be a God of Chaos or the Wyld, or are we stuck with guys like Plentimon (who's cool all on his own)<br /> <br /> Basically I want a Chaos Exalted, with Chaos and Probability-related charms because of reading Graceful Wicked Masques (which is pretty evocative, imo). How would I go about doing this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9947-blackwoodcoven","name":"BlackwoodCoven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T03:49:20-08:00","id":1055161,"title":"","content":"Ehhhh, if you want charms with Wyld-theme, can you just play...............Fair Folk ?<br /> <br /> Not to mention that Exigent can only be use by gods going by quotes from the writer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T05:33:19-08:00","id":1055187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackwoodCoven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld#post1055157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then Ex3 comes in with the whole plotline of Exigence and black market exaltations and I wondered (once again) -- can the Fair Folk use Exigence to create Exalted of their own?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope - only those lesser gods who use the Exigence can produce Exigents - an Exalt created by a Fair Folk would be something else.<br /> <br /> Mind, this isn't necessarily a bad thing - see below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackwoodCoven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld#post1055157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've read, there hasn't been anything explicit regarding whether Exigence can only be used by a God (unless there has been something explicit about that, then *sweat droopy*).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Sweat droopy&quot; it is - the devs have always been explicit that Exigents are the result of gods using the Exigence. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackwoodCoven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld#post1055157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is only usable by a God, would there be a God of Chaos or the Wyld, or are we stuck with guys like Plentimon (who's cool all on his own)</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that neither chaos nor the Wyld are people, neither would really be a very good fit for what Exigents are anyway. A god of chaos might make for a fun Exigent patron, mind - but you'd have to flesh him out more than just &quot;chaos,&quot; I think.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if you're not shackled to the whole &quot;as an Exigent&quot; concept, just think of a cool story for how a Fair Folk created her own Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackwoodCoven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld#post1055157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would I go about doing this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your game, dude - you're welcome to throw our advice in the trash and run what sounds fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-26-2017, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T05:37:46-08:00","id":1055191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackwoodCoven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld#post1055157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then Ex3 comes in with the whole plotline of Exigence and black market exaltations</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's also coming in with Liminals, Getimians and various others that haven't been named yet.<br /> <br /> I know that Exigence represents an especially tall and particularly lush tree, but there's still a forest surrounding it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T05:42:35-08:00","id":1055194,"title":"","content":"While the origin may be different, creating an Exigent of a god of Bad Luck or Ill Fortune might get you something of the same &quot;powerset&quot; you're looking for. Heck, even a god of Gambling or just Luck in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T06:03:21-08:00","id":1055205,"title":"","content":"Assuming we're sticking to an Exigent, you might be able to get what you want from Xaos the Hidden (Yu-Shan page 154).<br /> <br /> He's the God of Things Undiscovered who went behind enemy lines during the Balorian Crusade to gather intelligence and ended up losing his mind and these days mostly plays the role of a rambling oracle with rare lucid moments. Most intriguingly he claims to know &quot;the true name of the Wyld&quot; but can't seem to speak it and his attempts to do so have driven others insane. There's also a theory in Compass: Yu-Shan that he's more Unshaped than god now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T07:50:47-08:00","id":1055235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld?p=1055187#post1055187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, if you're not shackled to the whole &quot;as an Exigent&quot; concept, just think of a cool story for how a Fair Folk created her own Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Fair Folk Exalted sounds really cool. Dunno how I'd go about it though. The Fair Folk grabbed some Lunar Exalted, killed, them, trapped their Exaltations, and put them into Mortals of their own (sort of like how the Primordials did it I guess.)<br /> \u200b <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld?p=1055205#post1055205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming we're sticking to an Exigent, you might be able to get what you want from Xaos the Hidden (Yu-Shan page 154).<br /> <br /> He's the God of Things Undiscovered who went behind enemy lines during the Balorian Crusade to gather intelligence and ended up losing his mind and these days mostly plays the role of a rambling oracle with rare lucid moments. Most intriguingly he claims to know &quot;the true name of the Wyld&quot; but can't seem to speak it and his attempts to do so have driven others insane. There's also a theory in Compass: Yu-Shan that he's more Unshaped than god now.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is interesting and I might use it. His motivation even states that he &quot;wants to impart the terrible knowledge he gained all those years ago in the Wyld.&quot; Cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld?p=1055191#post1055191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt's also coming in with Liminals, Getimians and various others that haven't been named yet.<br /> <br /> I know that Exigence represents an especially tall and particularly lush tree, but there's still a forest surrounding it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can't wait for them too! But there aren't any Wyld/Chaos based Exalted so far, and I think it'll be a long time before more knowledge about the new Exalts comes into light.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it's fun to theorize that Solars have their counterpart to Abyssals, Sidereals to Getimians (probably), but Lunars don't. Now I know that not each Exalt NEEDS a counterpart, but I think it's fun to assume that if a Lunar did have a counterpart Exalt, it would be something based on chaotic stuff.<br /> <br /> \u200b <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9947-blackwoodcoven","name":"BlackwoodCoven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T12:26:33-08:00","id":1055345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackwoodCoven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld?p=1055235#post1055235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, I think it's fun to theorize that Solars have their counterpart to Abyssals, Sidereals to Getimians (probably)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold it. Nothing has even hinted at Sidereals becoming Getimians by any process. The Getimians were hidden somewhere, Thulio found them after he cut dies with destiny, and some renegade Sidereals sided with Thulio. At no point in this story do we get &quot;corrupted Sidereals&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , but Lunars don't. Now I know that not each Exalt NEEDS a counterpart, but I think it's fun to assume that if a Lunar did have a counterpart Exalt, it would be something based on chaotic stuff. </div> </div> </div>We already had that in 2e chimerae. It didn't work out well at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T13:24:02-08:00","id":1055366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackwoodCoven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld?p=1055235#post1055235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I can't wait for them too! But there aren't any Wyld/Chaos based Exalted so far, and I think it'll be a long time before more knowledge about the new Exalts comes into light.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSomething to keep in mind about Exigents; the information we wind up getting to help us come up with our own Exalted can be applied to ones who aren't Exigents, because the only thing that Exigents have in common is defined by plot.<br /> <br /> \u200bOnce the rules are there (or if somebody already has their own ideas), the origin can be anything that one wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T03:36:29-08:00","id":1055584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1055157-an-exigent-of-chaos-wyld?p=1055345#post1055345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold it. Nothing has even hinted at Sidereals becoming Getimians by any process. The Getimians were hidden somewhere, Thulio found them after he cut dies with destiny, and some renegade Sidereals sided with Thulio. At no point in this story do we get &quot;corrupted Sidereals&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9947-blackwoodcoven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9947_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9947\" data-vbnamecard=\"9947\">BlackwoodCoven</a> meant the way Getimians seem to be set up to be anti-Sids in terms of their aesthetics and powers without implying their origin story mirrors that of the Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}